@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+Feature: Clear completed todos
+  As a user
+  I want to remove all completed todos at once
+  So that I can clean up my list quickly
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes all completed todos
+    Given a completed todo "First" exists
+    And a todo "Second" exists
+    And a completed todo "Third" exists
+    When the user clicks the clear-completed button
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And todo "Second" exists
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when there are no completed todos
+    Given a todo "First" exists
+    Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when there are completed todos
+    Given a completed todo "First" exists
+    Then the clear-completed button is visible
diff --git a/features/counter.feature b/features/counter.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d99da73
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/counter.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+Feature: Active todo counter
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many todos are still active
+  So that I know how much work remains
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows zero when no todos exist
+    Then the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows the number of active todos
+    Given a todo "First" exists
+    And a completed todo "Second" exists
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter uses plural form for more than one active todo
+    Given a todo "First" exists
+    And a todo "Second" exists
+    Then the counter shows "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter updates when a todo is completed
+    Given a todo "First" exists
+    And a todo "Second" exists
+    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "First"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter updates when a todo is removed
+    Given a todo "First" exists
+    And a todo "Second" exists
+    When the user clicks the destroy button on todo "First"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
diff --git a/features/edit-todo.feature b/features/edit-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5449c83
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/edit-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+Feature: Edit a todo
+  As a user
+  I want to double-click a todo to edit its title
+  So that I can correct or update what I need to do
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo activates editing mode
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+    Then todo "Buy milk" has the editing class
+    And the edit input for todo "Buy milk" contains "Buy milk"
+    And the edit input for todo "Buy milk" is focused
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edit
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then todo "Buy oat milk" exists
+    And todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+
+  Scenario: Blurring the edit input saves the edit
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input and blurs
+    Then todo "Buy oat milk" exists
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace on save
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "  Buy oat milk  " in the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Saving an empty edit removes the todo
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "" in the edit input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Escape discards the edit
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user types "Changed" in the edit input and presses Escape
+    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..04b7ae5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+Feature: LocalStorage persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist when I reload the page
+  So that I do not lose my work
+
+  Rule: Todos survive a page reload
+
+    Scenario: Todos persist after reload
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a completed todo "Walk the dog" exists
+      When the app is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains 2 items
+      And todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And todo "Walk the dog" exists
+      And todo "Walk the dog" has the completed class
+
+    Scenario: Editing persists after reload
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input and presses Enter
+      And the app is reloaded
+      Then todo "Buy oat milk" exists
+      And todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+
+    Scenario: Removal persists after reload
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
+      When the user clicks the destroy button on todo "Buy milk"
+      And the app is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And todo "Walk the dog" exists
