diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..164507d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+Feature: Hash-based routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todos by All, Active, or Completed
+  So that I can focus on the subset I care about
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given a todo "Active" exists
+    And a completed todo "Done" exists
+    Then the selected filter is "All"
+    And the todo list contains 2 items
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    Given a todo "Active" exists
+    And a completed todo "Done" exists
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the selected filter is "Active"
+    And the todo list contains 1 item
+    And todo "Active" exists
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    Given a todo "Active" exists
+    And a completed todo "Done" exists
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the selected filter is "Completed"
+    And the todo list contains 1 item
+    And todo "Done" exists
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo hides it from the Active filter
+    Given the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Uncompleting a todo hides it from the Completed filter
+    Given the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    And a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists across reload
+    Given a todo "Active" exists
+    And a completed todo "Done" exists
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the selected filter is "Active"
+    And the todo list contains 1 item
diff --git a/features/toggle-todo.feature b/features/toggle-todo.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d06dd99
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle-todo.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+Feature: Toggle todo completion
+  As a user
+  I want to mark a todo as complete or active
+  So that I can track my progress
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox marks a todo as completed
+    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
+    Then todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox again marks a completed todo as active
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
+    Then todo "Buy milk" does not have the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete toggles all todos
+    Given a todo "First" exists
+    And a todo "Second" exists
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then todo "First" has the completed class
+    And todo "Second" has the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete is checked when all todos are completed
+    Given a completed todo "First" exists
+    And a completed todo "Second" exists
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete is unchecked when some todos are active
+    Given a completed todo "First" exists
+    And a todo "Second" exists
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking mark-all unchecks all todos
+    Given a completed todo "First" exists
+    And a completed todo "Second" exists
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then todo "First" does not have the completed class
+    And todo "Second" does not have the completed class
